  "type": "MCQ",
  "options": {
    "A": "Algorithm X is faster for $n = 100$ elements",
    "B": "Algorithm X is faster for $n = 1000$ elements",
    "C": "Algorithm Y is faster for any value of $n$",
    "D": "Algorithm X is faster for $n = 10$ elements"
  },
  "correct_answer": "C",
  "explanation": "To determine which algorithm is faster, we need to compare their time complexities. Algorithm X uses insertion sort, which has a time complexity of $O(n^2)$, while Algorithm Y uses merge sort, which has a time complexity of $O(n \log n)$. Since $n \log n$ grows faster than $n^2$ for large values of $n$, Algorithm Y is faster for any value of $n$."
