  "question": "Consider a comparison-based sorting algorithm that uses a modified merge sort strategy. In the worst-case scenario, the height of the recursion tree for this algorithm is $n$ (where $n$ is the number of elements to be sorted). If the time complexity of the merge step is $O(k)$, where $k$ is the number of elements being merged, then the worst-case time complexity of this algorithm is",
